`theorem_4_4_sourceTopology_homeomorph` transports the [Scott homeomorphism](1972_scottTopology.md) along the agreement of the inverse-limit Scott topology with the product subspace topology and of the function-space Scott topology with the pointwise topology (`theorem_3_3_topology_induced_pi`). The statement that uses it is [theorem_4_4](1972_theorem_4_4.md). Scott states one homeomorphism between \(D_\infty\) and \([D_\infty\to D_\infty]\), with the inverse limit carrying the subspace topology induced from the product and the function space carrying the pointwise topology of Definition 3.1. **Theorem:** yes — those are the topologies of the homeomorphism. **Proof:** partial — the underlying maps are Scott's pair, while the topology transport is an additional argument.
